fujinet-go-sms-desktop -- milestone log
======================================

The plan is the family's (see fujinet-go-adam-desktop/PORTING.md): one C API
in core/, four native frontends, FujiNet in-process, one shared settings
store, a native debugger everywhere, no panels visible at startup,
clone-and-build CI. The core is MAME's Master System transposed to C, the
astrocade sibling's way. Nothing below is marked done on "it compiles".

M0  scaffold                                                          [x]
  [x] root CMakeLists (VERSION 0.1.0, FRONTEND switch, WITH_SMS_ROMS OFF,
      no_embedded_roms registration, icon loop, CPack DEB/RPM/TGZ),
      .gitignore, LICENSE, tools/fujinet, mingw toolchain
  [x] cmake/Dependencies.cmake pins fujinet-firmware add-sms (b96613f, the
      Phantasy Star-style CONFIG; was 296ba263);
      FUJINET_SRC override; cmake/StageFujiProto.cmake stages pico/sms
  [x] tools/fujinet: BoIP 11508, web UI 11509; patch 0002 adds .sms/.sg to
      the RS232 ROM media type so CONFIG's MOUNT_IMAGE pushes them
  [x] vendored: z80.h/z80dasm.h (floooh, zlib), ymfm (MAME 3rdparty, BSD-3)
  [x] icons: the family mark in white on #E4002B over the cartridge-label
      grid (tools/icons/make-icons.py)

M1  emulator core (core/sms/), headless                               [x]
  [x] machine.c: the six models (sms1, sms1pal, sms, smspal, smsj,
      sg1000m3), memory map, BIOS paging, $3E/$3F, the Japanese and Mark III
      I/O maps, the smsj's C-Sync counter and Rapid button, the FM unit
  [x] vdp.c: 315-5124/5246, MAME's timers as a per-line event engine run
      against the CPU's cycle count; modes 0-4, sprites, flags, palettes
  [x] psg.c (SEGAPSG), fm_ym2413.cpp (ymfm), mix to 48 kHz stereo float
  [x] host.c: thread, NTSC/PAL pacing, vsync phase lock, frame slot, audio
  [x] calibrated against MAME with probe ROMs (tools/ab/probes): the beam's
      rounding (BEAM_ROUND_MCLK 0) and the IRQ look-ahead (IRQ_AHEAD 1);
      V/H counters at every line phase and every interrupt entry match
  [x] tools/ab/mame_ab.py: CONFIG, the probes and 76 games from the local
      corpus pixel-identical to MAME over 2400 frames of scripted play;
      sms, smspal, sms1pal, sg1000m3 too; real BIOS boots (bios13,
      alexkidd, jbios21 + the YM2413 patch ROM) identical

M2  FujiNet cartridge device                                          [x]
  [x] fujinet_cart.c: line-for-line transposition of emu/fujinet.cpp with
      real /M1 and the bus snoop; FN_R_LINK published as the firmware does
  [x] mailbox worker thread (the cart's core0), publish shadow, sync mode
  [x] fujitcp_host.c: portable transport with abort and EOF handling
  [x] tests: cart_seam (Sega and Codemasters routing, GAME vs APP, the GO
      flip only on a committed /M1 fetch of $0000, re-plan on /RESET, inert
      peeks, the $DFFC-$DFFF RAM copy), bios_synth (an in-test BIOS: the
      hand-over, the snoop, ANDed reads, 128K paging vs the smsj's, $3E's
      I/O-chip and work-RAM bits), fujibus_smoke, netboot with the mailbox
      on its worker and inline (fujiboot -> hello.sms through the SD host,
      then the 80K fujibank app opened directly)
  [x] ThreadSanitizer: clean over session, debug, gamepad, media,
      boot_smoke, fujibus_smoke and both netboots (build-tsan, local)

M3  session layer                                                     [x]
  [x] smssession.h: lifecycle, open/eject/soft reset/reset to CONFIG, the
      remembered cartridge, .cfg mapper overrides, Import Cartridge to SD
      (with the .cfg), import routing, Import BIOS by size + CRC with the
      custom-BIOS warning, per-console BIOS choice, the YM2413 patch ROM,
      bindings, gamepads, the FujiNet runtime, status
  [x] the host's run lock: every UI-thread look at the machine or the cart
      waits for the frame in progress instead of racing it; inputs are
      atomics latched at VBLANK
  [x] tests: session, media, bindings, gamepad, boot_smoke (CONFIG paints;
      59.92 / 49.70 Hz measured)

M4  debugger engine                                                   [x]
  [x] smsdebug.h: attach/stop/resume, step/over/out/run-to/scanline/frame,
      exec/read/write/in/out breakpoints with conditions, registers incl.
      shadows, memory/VRAM/CRAM, VDP decode and the four views, PSG/FM/I/O,
      the cartridge tab, built-in + WLA-DX/z88dk/SDCC/plain symbols (banked),
      trace ring, Save, the prompt with completion
  [x] tests: debug, dasm, vdp_decode, vdp_timing (MAME goldens)

M5-M8 frontends: GNOME, KDE, Windows, macOS                           [x]
  Ported from the NES sibling's, file by file: display (TV aspect 8:7 NTSC /
  1.386 PAL, smooth), menus (Machine / View / FujiNet / Help), Preferences
  (console, BIOS + Import BIOS, FM unit, audio, input, FujiNet), Controllers
  (two SMS joypads, Pause / Reset / Soft Reset / Reset to CONFIG, gamepads,
  Map, Defaults), the debugger (Prompt, CPU & RAM, Disassembly, VDP,
  Sound & I/O, Breakpoints, Cart), the FujiNet console log; SMS_OPEN_* hooks.
  [x] GNOME, KDE: no warnings, desktop + metainfo validated, smoke-launched
      headless (Broadway / offscreen) with every window open
  [x] Windows: cross-built with mingw-w64, no warnings; native MSYS2 build
      and tests green on CI
  [x] macOS: compiled and tested on CI, arm64 and x86_64 (never run on a
      Mac yet; the runners' coarse sleeps are reported, not asserted)
M9  packaging                                                         [x]
  [x] build-aux/flatpak/online.fujinet.go.sms.{gnome,kde}.yml (GNOME 49 /
      KDE 6.11, SDL3 3.4.12, firmware + mbedTLS pinned, -DWITH_SMS_ROMS=OFF);
      the core + libfujinet part built locally in the offline sandbox
  [x] build-aux/windows/installer.nsi (FujiNetGoSMS, per-user)
  [x] CPack per frontend (top-level), macOS bundle (frontends/macos)
M10 CI/CD                                                             [x]
  [x] linux.yml, windows.yml (green since M0)
  [x] macos.yml (arm64 + x86_64), flatpak.yml, release.yml (dry run on
      workflow_dispatch; draft release only for a v* tag)
  [x] linux, windows, macos (arm64 + x86_64), flatpak (gnome + kde) green
      with the frontends in
  [x] release.yml dry run (workflow_dispatch) green: the Linux packages for
      both frontends, both Flatpak bundles, the Windows zip and installer,
      the macOS zips for arm64 and x86_64; no release made, no tag pushed
      (MSYS2's NSIS 3.13 moved its plugins: the step finds nsDialogs and
      targets the architecture it was built for)
  Fixed on the way: the FujiNet DLL's static teardown double-freed the SD
  host's directory cache at exit (Windows crash after CONFIG listed SD) --
  the desktop entry releases the hosts first; boot_smoke gates the 2%
  rate check on the OS sleeping accurately (the macOS runners don't).
M11 family audit                                                      [x]
  The tree diffed against the NES and ColecoVision siblings with the
  machine names normalised away; added what was missing and not another
  machine's hardware: gamepad_map (an SDL3 virtual gamepad end to end) and
  store screenshots in both metainfo files. README "How this was verified"
  written from what actually ran.

Not yet done (needs hardware or a person):
  - run the Windows and macOS builds on a real desktop
  - (v0.1.0: tagged 2026-10-08, with the Phantasy Star-style CONFIG)

Verification beyond ctest (local):
  [x] tools/ab/audio_ab.py: FM (smsj, Mark III FM unit) and PSG (NTSC, PAL)
      sound matches MAME's
  [x] CONFIG driven like a user boots hello.sms from the SD host
      (tools: sms_drive; test: config_boot)
  [x] the core and session tests pass under Wine (mingw-w64 cross-build)
